rule (absolute offset not printed). Sensitivity is the reciprocal of the exposure (J/cm2) needed for a specified density (minimum density + 1.0). All curves are black; besides b/g/r the plot has the dashed curve of the fourth colour layer (\u7b2c4\u306e\u611f\u8272\u5c64, cyan-sensitive layer), traced as line l4 (build.py ignores it). Each layer curve ends in near-vertical drops, so the last few nm are approximated on the 5 nm grid.","Spectral dye density plot has only 'mid' (\u4e2d\u9593\u6fc3\u5ea6, density given by a neutral subject) and 'min' (\u6700\u5c0f\u6fc3\u5ea6, minimum density), no separate c/m/y dyes; the curves run 400-720 nm.","Grain: diffuse RMS granularity 7 (printed as '\u2026\u20267' next to heading 10); micro-densitometer aperture 48 um, sample density minimum density + 1.0. Film speed ISO 1600/33 deg daylight (tungsten 3200 K: ISO 400 with LBB-12). No paper is recommended on the sheet."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","grain":{"grain":28.0,"grain_size":44.0,"grain_roughness":50.0}}